{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a079c9-a389-7b22-a682-8d880628647c"},"sequence":327,"recorded_at":1780531400000649,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"15fbab40-2656-4b01-9f2b-97bf36f3de82","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"15fbab40-2656-4b01-9f2b-97bf36f3de82","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"15fbab40-2656-4b01-9f2b-97bf36f3de82"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"fb040c5e-e845-4112-8b7a-47a050354822"},"task_id":"fb040c5e-e845-4112-8b7a-47a050354822","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"fb040c5e-e845-4112-8b7a-47a050354822","span_id":"aec9625a5d7dd73b"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a079c9-a389-7b22-a682-8d880628647c"},"sequence":328,"recorded_at":1780531400000651,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"15fbab40-2656-4b01-9f2b-97bf36f3de82","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"15fbab40-2656-4b01-9f2b-97bf36f3de82","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"15fbab40-2656-4b01-9f2b-97bf36f3de82"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"fb040c5e-e845-4112-8b7a-47a050354822"},"task_id":"fb040c5e-e845-4112-8b7a-47a050354822","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"fb040c5e-e845-4112-8b7a-47a050354822","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/.agents/skills/project-management/references/change-request-lifecycle.md`.\n1|# Change Request Lifecycle Runbook\n2|\n3|Orchestrator-owned. An accepted Change Request is accepted work, not delivered\n4|work. This page states the order, the recovery paths, and the republish\n5|semantics that used to live only in an operator's head.\n6|\n7|The full typed contract — how a candidate is snapshotted, what\n8|`repository_delta` means, what a `stale` revision is, and every refusal you can\n9|hit — stays in\n10|[tracked background spawn](tracked-background-spawn.md), section\n11|`Change Requests, review, rework, and checkpoint`. This page is the order of\n12|operations on top of it.\n13|\n14|---\n15|\n16|## The Change Request lifecycle, in order\n17|\n18|1. **Accept.** The reviewer runs\n19|   `task-board m 'accept_cr(<ELEMENT-ID>, revision=<N>, evidence=<ELEMENT-ID>_review-verdict.md)'`.\n20|   The element parks at `to-review`. It is accepted, not delivered. Only the\n21|   reviewer run that was handed the revision may accept it.\n22|2. **Checkpoint immediately.** For every non-final leaf, run\n23|   `task-board worktree checkpoint <ELEMENT-ID>` as the next action after\n24|   acceptance. The accepted tree lands on the Story branch only, and the leaf\n25|   moves to `done`. Delay here is what makes the next producer's Change Request\n26|   go `stale`.\n27|3. **Refresh the index after every checkpoint.** A stale index is what makes the\n28|   next `integrate` disagree with the board.\n29|4. **Final leaf: integrate, do not checkpoint.** `checkpoint` refuses the\n30|   Story's last open leaf with `change_request_final_leaf_checkpoint`, because\n31|   closing it would promote a Story whose branch has never reached trunk. Land\n32|   the Story with\n33|   `task-board worktree integrate <STORY-ID> --cr <ELEMENT-ID> --revision <N>`.\n34|5. **When `integrate` refuses, report the refusal.** `validation_not_configured`\n35|   (`BUG-260807-1o5092`, the as-shipped behavior) and\n36|   `integration_indeterminate` for a board that lives outside the control root\n37|   are blockers, not detours. Report the refusal as the blocker it is and land\n38|   only by the documented manual signed substitute — an isolated clone, signed\n39|   cherry-pick of the exact reviewed head, a platform review record, and a\n40|   fail-closed plain push. Never route around a typed refusal by moving board\n41|   files or the branch by hand.\n42|6. **A lost run is recovered by republish, never by re-running the producer.** A\n43|   run that died after producing content but before the board recorded it still\n44|   has its content on disk. Republish it with provenance. Re-running the\n45|   producer discards work that already exists and costs the run again.\n46|7. **A republish of an unchanged accepted tree is an annotation, not a new\n47|   revision.** A candidate whose `repository_delta` is byte-identical to the\n48|   accepted one, and whose acceptance still stands, is not a new candidate.\n49|   Recording it as a revision turns the revision count — the only rework\n50|   measure the board has — into process noise.\n51|8. **Never commit manually on the Story branch.** The managed worktree's tree is\n52|   published by the producer's handoff and landed by `checkpoint` or\n53|   `integrate`. A hand commit on that branch makes the accepted snapshot and the\n54|   branch head disagree, and the disagreement surfaces later as an unexplained\n55|   `stale` or an integration that lands the wrong tree.\n56|\n57|## Two same-class findings mean a missing gate\n58|\n59|When two consecutive reviews of one leaf raise the same finding class, stop\n60|routing another rework revision. Spawn one task to add a gate for the class — a\n61|conformance vector set, a checker, a mutant harness — and let the next revision\n62|be reviewed against the gate rather than against a reviewer's memory. The\n63|reviewer's `repeat-of:` verdict field is the signal to route on.\n64|\n65|## Recovery surfaces\n66|\n67|- Stopped or refused integration: `task-board worktree transaction show <STORY-ID>`,\n68|  then the disposition surface it names.\n69|- A leaf whose handoff guard refused for artifact naming: attach the correctly\n70|  named `<ELEMENT-ID>_<slug>.<ext>` outcome resource and re-run the handoff. Do\n71|  not respawn the producer to satisfy a naming rule."}}}
